{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","index":0,"message":{"content":"I now have strong evidence for the key facts. Let me verify the remaining pieces:\n\n1. **Chigozie Obioma** was born in Akure, Nigeria (e1)\n2. His novels \"The Fishermen\" (2015) and \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" (2019) were shortlisted for the Booker Prize and translated into 30 languages (e1)\n3. **Marlon James** won the 2015 Booker Prize for \"A Brief History of Seven Killings\" (e2, search results)\n4. \"A Brief History of Seven Killings\" was published in 2014 (search results d71, d100, d101)\n5. Marlon James was born in Kingston, Jamaica (search results d95, d97)\n\nThe logic now fits perfectly:\n- The award is the **Booker Prize** (the question's \"originally created in the 2000s\" likely refers to the Man Group sponsorship era beginning 2002, or is a slight imprecision)\n- \"The Fishermen\" (2015) was shortlisted for the 2015 Booker Prize\n- In 2015 (the year \"The Fishermen\" was published), \"A Brief History of Seven Killings\" won the Booker Prize\n- \"A Brief History of Seven Killings\" was released in 2014 (the preceding year)\n- Marlon James (author of the prize-winning book) was born in Kingston, Jamaica\n- The question states the prize-winning author was born in the same city where the first author (Obioma) **grew up**\n\nSo I need to confirm: Did Chigozie Obioma grow up in Kingston, Jamaica? That seems unlikely for a Nigerian author. Let me verify where Obioma grew up, and also confirm Marlon James's birthplace with a direct read.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"ref\": \"d95\"}","name":"read"},"id":"call_a088f2fbaa5b4f94beb61627","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Chigozie Obioma grew up Akure Nigeria childhood hometown\", \"Chigozie Obioma biography early life Akure raised\", \"Marlon James born Kingston Jamaica biography\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_b253fe442ebb45e2920254b5","index":1,"t